        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Beech, Daviesia, Bitter-peas\n- Taxonomy: Fagus, Fagaceae, legume family\n- Places: Europe, Asia, North America, Australia, Western Australia\n\nFacts:\n- Beech, or Fagus, is a genus of deciduous trees in the family Fagaceae.\n- Beech is native to temperate Europe, Asia, and North America.\n- Daviesia, commonly known as Bitter-peas, is a large genus of flowering plants in the legume family.\n- Daviesia is native to Australia.\n- Daviesia has a center of diversity in Western Australia.",
